Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 08:59:07 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] mac80211: ath11k: add low memory RX profile for FW memory
 mode 2

Boards that select FW memory mode 2 (256 MB of RAM) still get the RX
rings sized for 1 GB boards, and their page_frag based RX buffers keep
pinning memory until the OOM killer takes hostapd and netifd down.

Shrink the RX refill and monitor rings and allocate one slab object
per RX buffer when FW memory mode 2 is selected. Other modes are not
affected. Details and measurements are in the patch description.

Signed-off-by: Alle4you <56454046+Alle4you@users.noreply.github.com>
